IMPORT prelude

-- Civil Aviation Authority of Singapore Act 2009 (Singapore) -- the airport licence and its offences (ss 36, 41, 42), control of
-- airport licensees (ss 56B, 57), the Authority's immunities and secrecy (ss 13, 14), enforcement offences and composition (ss 77,
-- 78, 79, 82, 85, 99), the airport development levy (s 87A), and statutory liens on aircraft (ss 89, 92, 93, 94, 95).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/CAASA2009.txt ("Current version
-- as at 01 Oct 2026" per the deposit's metadata), with amendments to Act 16 of 2025 (in force 1 October 2026) shown. Section numbers
-- follow the BODY of the deposit: in Part 9 the arrangement of sections is out of step with it (the body has the airport development
-- levy at s 87A, the SAF levy at s 87B, statutory liens at s 89 and the lien offence at s 94).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 7 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the rules with decision content that a
-- would-be airport operator, investor, airline or member of the public meets. Not encoded: the constitution, functions and finances
-- of the Authority (Parts 2, 2A), the 2009 transfer to the successor company (Part 3), licence conditions, modification, revocation
-- and security deposits (ss 37 to 40), codes of practice, the reserve fund, master plans and charges (ss 44 to 54), appeals (ss 55,
-- 56), designated operating entities (Part 5 Division 3), by-laws and abandoned aircraft (Part 6), slot coordination (Part 6A),
-- special administration (Part 7), the general levy and SAF levy beyond their mention (ss 86, 87, 87B), and the levy rates, which are
-- set by Gazette order and were not retrieved.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Civil Aviation Authority of Singapore Act 2009 -- airports`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the smaller of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the larger of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT LEAST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `36 -- operating an airport`

-- s 36(1): "A person must not operate an airport unless the person is authorised to do so by -- (a) an airport licence; or (b) an
-- exemption granted by the Authority under section 43."
-- (6): a fine "not exceeding $1 million and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not exceeding $25,000 for every
-- day or part of a day during which the offence continues after conviction". No imprisonment is provided.
GIVEN `operates an airport` IS A BOOLEAN, `holds an airport licence` IS A BOOLEAN, `holds a section 43 exemption` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `operating the airport is an offence` IF
    `operates an airport` AND (NOT `holds an airport licence`) AND (NOT `holds a section 43 exemption`)

-- "day or part of a day": a part day counts as a whole day, so the caller passes whole days (rounded up).
GIVEN `days continued after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 36 maximum fine` MEANS
    1000000 PLUS 25000 TIMES `days continued after conviction`

§§ `41, 42 -- transfer of the licence and non-airport business`

-- s 41(1): "No airport licence may be transferred to any person without the prior consent in writing of the Authority." (2): a
-- purported transfer in contravention "is void and of no effect".
GIVEN `the Authority consented in writing beforehand` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the licence transfer is effective` IF
    `the Authority consented in writing beforehand`

-- s 42(1): except with the Authority's prior approval, a licensee "must not carry on substantial trading or financial activities"
-- other than activities relating to or incidental to operating the airport and consistent with the lease and master plan.
-- (2): not for a person who acquires the airport-site lease "by way of the enforcement of a loan security". (3): "A contravention of
-- this section does not affect the validity of any transaction." (No penalty is stated in s 42; s 99 is the general penalty for
-- offences with none expressly provided -- whether a s 42 contravention is an offence at all is not stated, and is not encoded.)
GIVEN `substantial non-airport activity` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Authority approved it beforehand` IS A BOOLEAN, `acquired the lease by enforcing a loan security` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the licensee contravenes s 42` IF
    `substantial non-airport activity` AND (NOT `the Authority approved it beforehand`) AND (NOT `acquired the lease by enforcing a loan security`)

§§ `56B, 57 -- becoming a 5% controller of an airport licensee`

-- s 56B(2): for an airport licensee (not also a designated entity), a "5% controller" is a person who, with associates, "(a) holds
-- 5% or more of the total equity interests ... or (b) is in a position to control 5% or more of the voting power". (3): the Minister
-- may by Gazette order specify a HIGHER percentage. The threshold is therefore a parameter (5 unless varied).
-- s 56B(1): for a designated entity the band is "5% or more, but less than 25%".
GIVEN `equity percent` IS A NUMBER, `voting percent` IS A NUMBER, `threshold percent` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a 5% controller of an airport licensee` IF
    `equity percent` AT LEAST `threshold percent` OR `voting percent` AT LEAST `threshold percent`

GIVEN `equity percent` IS A NUMBER, `voting percent` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a 5% controller of a designated entity` IF
        (`equity percent` AT LEAST 5 AND `equity percent` LESS THAN 25)
    OR  (`voting percent` AT LEAST 5 AND `voting percent` LESS THAN 25)

-- s 57(1): a person must not "become a 5% controller or an indirect controller of an airport licensee ... without obtaining the
-- prior written approval of the Authority". (2): approval if the person is "fit and proper", the licensee will continue to conduct
-- its business prudently, and "it is in the public interest to do so" -- all three. ("may approve": satisfying them permits approval,
-- it does not compel it.)
GIVEN `fit and proper` IS A BOOLEAN, `licensee will stay prudent and compliant` IS A BOOLEAN, `in the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Authority may approve the controller` IF
    `fit and proper` AND `licensee will stay prudent and compliant` AND `in the public interest`

-- s 57(7): a defence for the person to prove "(a) the person was not aware that the person had contravened subsection (1); OR (b)
-- ... within a period of 14 days after becoming aware" notified the Authority and took the actions the Authority directed.
-- (8): also a defence, though aware, if the breach arose from an ASSOCIATE's increase, there is no agreement or arrangement with that
-- associate, and the person notified within 14 days after the contravention and took directed action. (10): otherwise lack of
-- intent or knowledge is no defence.
GIVEN `became a controller without approval` IS A BOOLEAN, `was unaware of the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN, `days to notify after becoming aware` IS A NUMBER, `took the directed action` IS A BOOLEAN, `caused by an associate without arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN, `days to notify after the contravention` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 57(1) offence is made out` IF
        `became a controller without approval`
    AND (NOT `was unaware of the contravention`)
    AND (NOT (`days to notify after becoming aware` AT MOST 14 AND `took the directed action`))
    AND (NOT (`caused by an associate without arrangement` AND `days to notify after the contravention` AT MOST 14 AND `took the directed action`))

-- s 57(5): the licensee must give the Authority written notice, within the prescribed time, of an acquisition making someone a 5%
-- controller. (9): a defence to prove the licensee "(a) was not aware ... AND (b) ... within a period of 5 days after becoming aware"
-- notified the Authority. Note "and" here against "or" in (7).
GIVEN `failed to notify in the prescribed time` IS A BOOLEAN, `licensee was unaware` IS A BOOLEAN, `days to notify after becoming aware` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 57(5) offence is made out` IF
    `failed to notify in the prescribed time` AND (NOT (`licensee was unaware` AND `days to notify after becoming aware` AT MOST 5))

-- s 57(6): (a) individual -- $500,000 or 3 years or both, plus $50,000 a day continuing after conviction; (b) any other case --
-- $1 million, plus $100,000 a day.
GIVEN `is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN, `days continued after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 57 maximum fine` MEANS
    IF `is an individual`
    THEN 500000 PLUS 50000 TIMES `days continued after conviction`
    ELSE 1000000 PLUS 100000 TIMES `days continued after conviction`

GIVEN `is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 57 maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    IF `is an individual` THEN 36 ELSE 0

§§ `13, 14 -- immunity and secrecy`

-- s 13(1): no suit lies against the Authority, its members, officers, employees or persons acting under its directions "for
-- anything which is in good faith done". (2): no action for loss of or damage to an aircraft during or after a seizure under s 92,
-- or "any economic loss suffered by a person as a result of such a seizure". (3): (2) "does not cover loss or damage that is
-- wilfully or negligently caused".
GIVEN `done in good faith under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN, `loss arose from a s 92 seizure` IS A BOOLEAN, `wilfully or negligently caused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Authority is immune from suit` IF
        `done in good faith under the Act`
    OR  (`loss arose from a s 92 seizure` AND (NOT `wilfully or negligently caused`))

-- s 14(1): a present or past member, officer, employee, adviser or agent must not disclose information obtained under the Act,
-- "except for the purpose of the performance of the person's duties ... or when lawfully required to do so by any court or where
-- required or allowed by" written law. (2): $2,000 or 6 months or both.
GIVEN `disclosed information obtained under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN, `for the performance of duties` IS A BOOLEAN, `required by a court` IS A BOOLEAN, `required or allowed by written law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the disclosure is a s 14 offence` IF
        `disclosed information obtained under the Act`
    AND (NOT `for the performance of duties`)
    AND (NOT `required by a court`)
    AND (NOT `required or allowed by written law`)

§§ `77, 78, 82, 94, 99 -- offence penalties`

-- s 77(1) wilfully damaging the Authority's property: $5,000 or 6 months or both (plus compensation on the Authority's application).
-- s 78(3) refusing access to or obstructing the Authority's officers: $2,000 or 3 months or both.
-- s 82(3) failing without reasonable excuse to comply with an information notice: $10,000 (fine only).
-- s 82(4) altering, suppressing or destroying documents, or a knowingly or recklessly false statement: $10,000 or 12 months or both.
-- s 94(4) removing or stripping an aircraft under statutory lien: $200,000 or 12 months or both.
-- s 14(2) unauthorised disclosure: $2,000 or 6 months or both.
-- s 99: an offence "for which no penalty is expressly provided" -- $5,000 or 6 months or both.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `damaging the Authority's property`
    `obstructing the Authority's officers`
    `ignoring an information notice`
    `falsifying or destroying information`
    `removing or stripping a liened aircraft`
    `unauthorised disclosure`
    `an offence with no stated penalty`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `damaging the Authority's property` THEN 5000
    WHEN `obstructing the Authority's officers` THEN 2000
    WHEN `ignoring an information notice` THEN 10000
    WHEN `falsifying or destroying information` THEN 10000
    WHEN `removing or stripping a liened aircraft` THEN 200000
    WHEN `unauthorised disclosure` THEN 2000
    OTHERWISE 5000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `damaging the Authority's property` THEN 6
    WHEN `obstructing the Authority's officers` THEN 3
    WHEN `ignoring an information notice` THEN 0
    WHEN `falsifying or destroying information` THEN 12
    WHEN `removing or stripping a liened aircraft` THEN 12
    WHEN `unauthorised disclosure` THEN 6
    OTHERWISE 6

§§ `79, 85 -- prosecution and composition`

-- s 79: "No court is to try any offence under this Act ... except with the consent of the Public Prosecutor."
GIVEN `the Public Prosecutor consented` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a court may try the offence` IF
    `the Public Prosecutor consented`

-- s 85(1): an offence PRESCRIBED as compoundable may be compounded "by collecting ... the lower of the following: (a) a sum not
-- exceeding one-half of the amount of the maximum fine that is prescribed for the offence; (b) $5,000." The prescription is in
-- regulations not retrieved; the encoding takes the maximum fine as given.
GIVEN `maximum fine for the offence` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the largest composition sum` MEANS
    `the smaller of` (`maximum fine for the offence` DIVIDED BY 2) 5000

§§ `87A -- airport development levy`

-- s 87A(1): the levy "is payable in respect of every air passenger ticket that covers at least one flight that takes off -- (a)
-- from an airport at Changi to a place outside Singapore; and (b) on or after a date specified by an order ... being no earlier than
-- 29 June 2018". (2): the amount or rate is prescribed by Gazette order (not retrieved). Dates are YYYYMMDD.
GIVEN `a flight on the ticket departs Changi for outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `departure date` IS A NUMBER, `order start date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the airport development levy is payable on the ticket` IF
        `a flight on the ticket departs Changi for outside Singapore`
    AND `departure date` AT LEAST (`the larger of` `order start date` 20180629)

§§ `89, 92, 93, 94, 95 -- statutory liens on aircraft`

-- s 89(1): if a levy or service charge "imposed in respect of an aircraft is not paid in full by the due date" and any part remains
-- unpaid, an authorised employee "may make an entry in the Register of Statutory Liens"; (2) the lien then vests in the Authority.
GIVEN `levy or charge unpaid after due date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a lien may be registered` IF
    `levy or charge unpaid after due date`

-- ss 92(1), 93(1): seizure, and sale or disposal, become available if an outstanding amount "remains unpaid at the end of 9 months
-- after the day on which it became an outstanding amount or the day on which the lien was registered, whichever is the later".
-- Months are counted as whole months elapsed.
GIVEN `months since it became outstanding` IS A NUMBER, `months since the lien was registered` IS A NUMBER, `still unpaid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the aircraft may be seized or sold` IF
    `still unpaid` AND (`the smaller of` `months since it became outstanding` `months since the lien was registered`) AT LEAST 9

-- s 94(1): a person who KNOWS a lien is in effect "must not remove the aircraft from Singapore"; (2) "must not detach any part or
-- equipment from the aircraft"; (3) not with prior approval of an authorised employee. (5): "For the purposes of establishing a
-- contravention of subsection (1)" -- removal ONLY -- a person is taken to have known "if the person ought reasonably to have known".
DECLARE LienAct IS ONE OF
    `removing the aircraft from Singapore`
    `detaching a part or equipment`
    `doing nothing to the aircraft`

GIVEN `the act` IS A LienAct, `knew of the lien` IS A BOOLEAN, `ought reasonably to have known` IS A BOOLEAN, `had prior approval` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the act is a s 94 offence` IF
    CONSIDER `the act`
    WHEN `removing the aircraft from Singapore` THEN (`knew of the lien` OR `ought reasonably to have known`) AND (NOT `had prior approval`)
    WHEN `detaching a part or equipment` THEN `knew of the lien` AND (NOT `had prior approval`)
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 95(1), (2): a person affected by a decision under s 89, 92 or 93 may apply in writing for reconsideration "within 28 days after
-- the day on which the decision first comes to the notice of the person, or within such further period as the Authority allows".
GIVEN `days after notice` IS A NUMBER, `further period allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the review application is in time` IF
    `days after notice` AT MOST (28 PLUS `further period allowed`)
